{"id": 11, "ts": 1779499808.0749514, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I\u2019d like to add two observations from my interview that have not yet been shared and that bear directly on the key criteria of stress resilience, technical competence, and crew cooperation.\n- **Candidate\u202fB** \u2013 In addition to the strengths already noted (conscientiousness, stress handling, weather assessment, computer skills), I observed that B has a relatively weak memory for numerical data and, on several occasions, made nasty remarks toward colleagues. Both points raise concerns about attention to detail and professional communication/crew\u2011cooperation, which are critical for long\u2011haul operations.\n- **Candidate\u202fC** \u2013 Beyond the dossier\u2019s emphasis on reliability and quick decision\u2011making, I saw that C remains calm in a crisis and demonstrates a solid grasp of complex technology. These traits reinforce C\u2019s stress resilience and technical competence, partially offsetting the documented communication and egocentricity concerns.\nGiven these additions, the trade\u2011off remains between B\u2019s overall technical and decision\u2011making strength versus C\u2019s reliability and calmness, each with notable crew\u2011cooperation issues. I suggest we obtain concrete examples of B\u2019s interaction style (e.g., simulator debrief feedback) and consider whether C\u2019s communication gaps can be mitigated through training before we finalize the recommendation.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce public message and metadata. As agent_2, we need to contribute next useful piece. We have already seen Agent1 and Agent3 contributions. We need to add something new: perhaps ask a tool question to get more info about crew cooperation for Candidate B or D, or share our own private notes not yet disclosed: we have private notes: Candidate A regarded as